title: c2c send CLI has no --deferrable flag (MCP-only) — CLI/MCP parity gap
updated_at: "2026-07-17T16:50:02Z"
---
During cross-host dogfood (2026-07-18): 'c2c send <alias> --deferrable <msg>' → 'unknown option --deferrable'. The deferrable flag exists only on the MCP send tool (documented docs/commands.md:139) and 'c2c relay dm send' has no deferrable/ephemeral/tag flags either. CLI-first clients (kimi's default path!) cannot send deferrable messages at all. Add --deferrable to 'c2c send' (and consider flag parity on 'c2c relay dm send').